> (3) as the true one on the incorrect altar
>
>       Can you still win the game?

If you do (3), then your god gets VERY mad, but the god you sacrificed it
to allows you to live. You dont become a demigod, and the game is over.
If you do (1) or (2), you either lose 1 luck if you dont know
that its fake (i.e. its no identified as fake) or 3 luck, 1 allignment,
and incur the anger of the appropriate god... In the case of (2),
the god zaps you, as if you tried to conver the high altar with
any other sacrifice, in the case of (1) you get typical god anger.
(this is from reading the source in pray.c)

As a side note: if you get to the stairs at level one, and go up
them with a fake amulet of yendor,  you will simply exit the dungeon,
and the game will be over- so be sure its the real one before 
you do this.  If you exit the dungeon instead of going to the planes
b/c of this, you wont be able to win (the game will end).

